# Calendar Days — a tear-off calendar (31 pages, 3D rotateX flips with per-page
# springs, depth shadows, face swap at 0.5) driven by a pan slider below it.
# What this test covers: a slow drag through the first pages (one flip at a
# time), a fast drag to the end (many pages flipping simultaneously), dragging
# past both ends of the track (clamped), a fast return to day 1 (all pages
# unflipping together), tiny back-and-forth drags across a single page
# boundary (spring retargeted repeatedly), a fling-like quick drag mid-way,
# and a tap on the track away from the thumb (must do nothing).
# Thumb starts at (40,562); track spans x 40-362.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/calendar-days"
wait "text" "ON THE" 10000
wait 1500
gesture pan 40 562 60 0 2000
wait 1200
gesture pan 100 562 262 0 400
wait 1500
# Past the end (clamped).
gesture pan 362 562 30 0 300
wait 800
# Fast back to day 1 and past the start.
gesture pan 362 562 -350 0 400
wait 2000
# Back and forth across one page boundary.
gesture pan 40 562 12 0 300
wait 150
gesture pan 52 562 -10 0 300
wait 150
gesture pan 42 562 12 0 300
wait 150
gesture pan 54 562 -12 0 300
wait 1500
# Mid-way quick drags.
gesture pan 42 562 160 0 200
wait 300
gesture pan 202 562 -80 0 200
wait 300
gesture pan 122 562 200 0 200
wait 2000
# Tap on the track far from the thumb.
press 120 562
wait 600
gesture pan 322 562 -300 0 600
wait 2000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 3000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\" id=\"xmark\""
wait 1500
